  "summary": "A common summer resident. The male is bright green above and white below, with white marks before and behind the eye, a white crown stripe, white marks on the wings, a black bill and a red eye. The female is more coppery above. The immature has a coral-red bill, blue eyes and spotted underparts. The male calls dee-dee-dee-deederik. The female calls deea-deea-DEEA. It parasitises weavers, bishops and sparrows. Months were left unset. The Kemp code VB was left unchanged.",
